  "articleBody": "It’s a fact: small roof issues can quickly become huge headaches, especially with the demanding Texas weather we experience. Catching these problems early can save you a ton of money and stress down the line. We believe in being proactive, and knowing what to look for can empower you as a homeowner to protect your biggest investment.\n\n- [ ] Check for missing, cracked, or curled shingles — these are obvious signs that your roof's protection is compromised and can lead to water intrusion.\n- [ ] Look for granular loss in gutters or on the ground — this indicates the protective layer of your shingles is eroding, reducing their lifespan and weather resistance.\n- [ ] Inspect your flashings around chimneys, vents, and skylights — damaged or poorly sealed flashing is a very common entry point for water leaks into your home.\n- [ ] Keep an eye out for signs of water stains or sagging on interior ceilings — these are critical indicators of active leaks that have made their way into your home's structure.\n- [ ] Note any moss or algae growth on your roof — while sometimes cosmetic, excessive growth can trap moisture, accelerate deterioration, and hide underlying damage.\n- [ ] Examine your gutters for clogs or signs of overflow — blocked gutters can cause water to back up, leading to fascia damage, foundation issues, and even roof deck rot.\n- [ ] Check for loose or exposed nails — these can allow water to seep under shingles, compromising the integrity of your roof and leading to leaks.\n\nHow to use this checklist:\nGo through these points periodically, especially after a big storm. If you spot any of these issues, it's probably time to call in a professional. Discounted Roofing Co. offers professional inspections and assessments to help you understand exactly what's going on up there and what your best options are.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}